  "target_identity": {
    "north_star": "La Nuit's cardamom-lavender-cedar recognizers carried in an intimate but breathing aura: one soft skin-musk function, Hedione and aromatic alcohol diffusion, and an Iso E halo—close, sensual, and legible rather than a clean musk curtain.",
    "functional_architecture": [
      "cardamom and lavender remain readable at the center",
      "one exact skin-musk function supplies intimacy without a chord",
      "Hedione, Ethyl Linalool, and Iso E provide diffusion so musk does not have to project the whole perfume",
      "cedar-vetiver-coumarin drydown remains materially legible"
    ],
    "protected_identity": [
      "Cardamom Oil",
      "Lavender",
      "Cedarwood Virginia",
      "Vetiver Haiti",
      "Coumarin"
    ],
    "primary_axis": "single-musk skin intimacy decoupled from transparent aromatic and molecular diffusion",
    "variant_socket": {
      "active_ppm_w_w": 66666.667,
      "current_raw_ul": 300,
      "target_allocation": {
        "Exaltolide increment": 18000,
        "Hedione increment": 16000,
        "Iso E Super increment": 12000,
        "Ethyl Linalool increment": 8000,
        "Cardamom increment": 6000,
        "Lavender increment": 4000,
        "Sandalwood increment": 2666.6666
      },
      "current_allocation_ul": {
        "Ethylene Brassylate": 80,
        "Hedione": 70,
        "Iso E Super": 50,
        "Ethyl Linalool": 30,
        "Cardamom EO": 30,
        "Lavender EO (BONTAUX SAS)": 20,
        "Sandalore": 20
      }
    },
    "selection_rationale": [
      "The inventory-independent ideal retains Exaltolide as La Nuit's exact soft skin target; the current build chooses EB as its one musk because EB is the only user-owned candidate with a working neat w/w basis.",
      "EB's creamy-lactonic continuity suits coumarin-tonka intimacy, while Hedione, Ethyl Linalool, and Iso E carry outward diffusion; EB is not asked to become a projection curtain.",
      "Romandolide was rejected for this current arm because its basis is unrecorded and its cleaner outward signature would change the test; Habanolide was rejected for the same basis gap and a warmer metallic skin fingerprint; Galaxolide, Zenolide, Ambrettolide, and depleted exception musks are excluded.",
      "No second musk is added; cedar, vetiver, coumarin, and tonka remain independently legible."
    ],
    "drift_risk": "More EB or any second musk could blur cardamom, lavender, and cedar into a generic clean or creamy curtain; too much Hedione would also hollow the heart."
  },
